Research loop 2 (HFT corpus: squawk-hft-latency.md, squawk-hft-microsecond.md,
hft-specs/, race skill) synthesized into the router:

- hedgedChain(): preferred lane gets a head start; if no winner within
  ESTATE_HEDGE_MS (1500ms), the whole remaining field races in parallel.
  First substantive wins; loser aborts are NOT circuit strikes. Lanes with
  recent strikes lose the lane-0 head start (still race at the hedge).
  HEDGE_MS=0 restores the sequential chain.
- routeAstRace(): first-substantive-wins (was allSettled — slowest lane set
  the pace). Losers aborted. isAst code-shaped output keeps priority via a
  250ms quality window.
- Latency-aware ordering: per-provider latency EMA (alpha 0.2) feeds
  candidateScore() = Elo - EMA_ms/50. Chronic slowness demotes a provider
  despite higher Elo.
- Per-hop telemetry: X-Estate-Timings (connect_ms/ttft_ms/total_ms) on
  every chat response; p50/p95 per provider in /status (SQLite, 30min).
- Push-not-poll kimi-auto: fs.watch on the resolver state.json keeps
  /status resolved_model instant; shim reads state live per request.
- Warm standby: 30s /models pings for local providers via
  state.recordProbe() — strikes + circuit only, no Elo inflation, no DB rows.
  Dead local backend quarantines before user traffic hits it.
- Streaming explicit-model failover: resolved lane first, then the weighted
  field (was: same single candidate retried, then 503).
- /status: circuit detail, last_error, latency_ms p50/p95, kimi resolved.

Also: v3.2 version stamp on /health; isRoutableModelId exported for reuse.

Tests: tests/hedge.test.ts, 8 pass (bun test) — hedge timing, loser-abort
isolation, strike demotion, spec normalization, quarantine, latency EMA.

Live evidence 2026-09-20: blackhole :25100 -> explicit bornite request
200 via nvidia (zero client failures); warm standby auto-quarantined the
dead backend; prober healed on recovery (open->half->closed). Shim
fail-fast: /home/toxic/kimi-auto/shim.py upstream timeout 120s -> 8s.

